  "CREATURE/DRAGONSPAWN2_MODULAR/DRAGONSPAWN2_MODULAR.M2": {
    "note": "I-392: retail dragonspawn2.m2 (1 view, so the client loads only DRAGONSPAWN2_MODULAR00.SKIN) plus retail dragonspawn2boss's pads and helm crest (donors/, FDID of creature/dragonspawn2boss/dragonspawn2boss.m2, converted by lib/retail.convert): its submesh 2 (armour, boss armour texture + reflect) and 3 (additive glow on UV2, imported static: our model has no UV animation) written over unused lower-LOD vertices from 16509 (sliced numbering), bones remapped onto this rig (same pivots; the boss's 4 pad flap bones ride their parents). Textures 3 = boss armour as replaceable type 13 (the display's 3rd skin slot: dragonspawn2boss_armor_<colour>, black = the retail gold), 4 = glow (fixed); texture lookup 4-5 = (boss armour, reflect), 6-7 = (glow, glow); material 4 = (21, 4) additive; texture unit lookup 2-3 = (0, 1). base_sha256 pins the donor. Vertex array sliced to 20030..39560 (LOD1's run + the boss pieces; m2.vertices.slice): the picker merges weapon/shield meshes into the model as extra vertices, which the u16 skin lookup cannot reach past 65,535 on the full 86k array. Wings (I-392, 2026-10-13): stock dragonspawngreater's spread (right) wing, bone subtree 27, mirrored, raised 0.4, re-centred 0.28 (the classic model sits 0.28 off the midline) and pulled 0.4 in over the shoulder blades, bound rigidly to key bone 53 (m2.import_rigid, vertices from 19531); textures 5-11 = DRAGONSPAWN2WING_<colour> (texture lookup 8-14); material 5 = (4, 1) two-sided alpha test. The wing arm and claw (strut: within 0.08 of the leading-edge UV line, or the claw box) get their own vertex copies with UVs along the body skin's tail strip, drawn with the body skin (texture lookup 0), so they wear the display's own scales.",
